  "title": "India's AI Infrastructure and Connectivity Expansion",
  "summary": "L&T and Nokia expand their partnership in India for R&D, establishing an offshore development center focused on 5G and AI. Tamil Nadu and India's AI data center developments in Hyderabad show growing collaboration in AI infrastructure. India's government plans to build 100 new airports and invest Rs 30,000 crore to enhance regional connectivity.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "L&T and Nokia have signed a five-year contract with India to support engineering and R&D in the country, including a dedicated offshore development center in India.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "Tamil Nadu and India's AI data center in Hyderabad, along with TCS subsidiary HyperVault, have established a ₹70,000 crore AI data center in collaboration with Singapore.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "The Indian government announced a ₹1.27 lakh crore Semicon 2.0 scheme to boost the chip manufacturing ecosystem across India.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
  ],
